< **Status summary (v0.3.22 DRAFT r3):** One new scientific cell, §6.13b (A1a), with eight proposed RIDs (registered only on adoption) and four artifact IDs (§8). On the explicit start set $U=\{0<Q_0\le\tfrac1{625}\}$, A1a's local extension $D_M^U$ of the Number Genesis defect formula aligns exactly with Dyadic's block phase, and $MQ_M\to1$; on the intersection with NUMGEN's existential tube $U_{\rm NUMGEN}$, $D_M^U$ equals NUMGEN's $D_M$. Hence: the limit $C_D^{\rm ext}=\lim_M(D_M^U-\tau\log M)$ exists and equals $\tau\log Q_0-M_W$ (`[THM]`, using RECOG's own R9 through Dyadic T1/T2); on $U\cap U_{\rm NUMGEN}$ it equals NUMGEN's $C_D$, and the asymptotic phase exists **without R9** (existence only, `[RESULT] [from: ALG]`, no explicit radius); quantitatively $C_D^{\rm ext}=\tau\log Q_0-\mathcal P_2(W_0)+E$ per Dyadic OPEN 21 row (`[THM]`). No existing scientific RID, grade or OPEN status changes; R6 stays ACTIVE. §7 gains the A1a import rows and a scope note on the NUMGEN defect-threshold row; §7.2 N13 is updated in three separate fields. **Release state:** integrated review of DRAFT r2 accepted (L1/L2 closed); A1a-G1 allocation resolved by the NUMGEN owner (option 1; co-owner ruling of 20 Oct 2026), canonical repin of the two NUMGEN imports pending NUMGEN v1.20.8; PI adoption pending.
